  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"{\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mo>;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mtd><mtd><mo>;</mo></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced></math> is differentiable at <math><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,</mn></math> then <math><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi></math> can be"
  },
